22-// opens a DRAFT claim in the person's claim form (cancel closes it again); editing any other claim, one whose due-by is inside a closed
23-// period, or one another user's open editor locks, is refused with the claim's error — to change an open claim, void it and
24-// add a new one. An open editor locks the claim for other users until it is saved or cancelled, or the sheet's today changes. A steward (or the roles the sheet's
25:// reassign permission allows) moves a DRAFT, OPEN or
26:// PENDING claim to another person on the sheet with the reassign button (it is listed first under them, live again until
27-// their next statement); a settled or voided claim, or a move by anyone else, is refused with the claim's error.
28-// A steward re-settles a SETTLED claim (outside any closed period) with the re-settle button: its due is frozen again at the
29-// figure it would have today as an open claim bound by no statement, and its log gains a SETTLED line; else it is refused with the claim's error.
30-// An OPEN claim is deferred to a date after the sheet's today with the defer date and button (a claim that is not OPEN, a date
31-// not after today or a claim dated inside a closed period is refused with the claim's error): until the sheet's today reaches
32-// that date it counts in no total, is not overdue, cannot be settled and is left unbound by a statement. Each claim shows
33-// deferred (yes while it is deferred) and the date it was deferred until.
34-// An OPEN or PENDING claim is reminded with the remind button, once per sheet-today: it shows the sheet's today as its reminded
35-// date (the last day a reminder was written, blank if never). A second reminder the same day, or a claim in any other status,
36-// is refused with the claim's error.
37-// A steward re-dates an OPEN or PENDING claim with the new date and re-date button: its due-by stays as it was fixed, a figure a
38-// statement bound it to stays bound, and, as its period goes by its due-by, it keeps its period and number. A date after the
39-// person's retirement, a claim whose due-by is inside a closed period, or a re-dating by anyone but a steward, is refused with the claim's error.
40-// Each claim shows its proofs count, raised by one with the proof button (a SETTLED or VOID claim, or one dated inside a closed
41-// period, is refused with the claim's error). A claim whose due is above the proof threshold in force on its date cannot be
42-// settled or approved while its proofs count is 0: that is refused with the claim's error, before the clerk limit is considered.
43-// An OPEN claim is split with the split amount (more than 0.00 and less than its amount) and button: it keeps the rest
44-// of its amount and loses any figure a statement bound it to, and a new OPEN claim with the split-off amount, the same
45-// date and note, the next number, opened by the user and its due-by fixed now is listed under the person, showing the
46-// original's number as split-from. A PENDING, deferred or settled claim, one dated inside a closed period, or a split by a
47-// role that may not open a claim, is refused with the claim's error.
48-// Each claim shows its status log, oldest first: one line per status it has had, with who set it, the sheet's today then and its due then.
49-// A claim is commented with the comment text and button (an empty comment is refused with the claim's error); its comments
50-// are shown oldest first, each as "<user> on <date>: <text>", the date being the sheet's today when it was written.
